# 40_rspec.kzp -- K-REG.osal-countsem-lookup at CF 281a941, as it stands (SPEC rev 1.3 App. A.4 steps 3
# and 6; plan/C1_basis_plan.md 9.3, 9.6).
#
# The readiness precondition applies to the dependent use of CF (role cf-dependent-lookup); BP's existence
# probe is not an instance (role bp-existence-probe, 10_kinds.kzp).  At 281a941 there is one lookup and no
# record that accepts or rejects the pre-fix handling (exit with APP_ERROR): the caller-level Allowed is
# unspecified_by_reference, so a not-ready lookup is NOT_READY_UNJUDGED, summary
# INCONCLUSIVE(caller_requirement_absent).  The open PI decision P3 (Q-12) could change this only through
# a caller record of the pre-fix handling; its alternative is ../rspec-281a941-altP3/, not the current
# reading.  The event, CF's exit and the harm are consequences, recorded apart.
# 2026-10-29 (PI decision, Architecture/spec/PI_DECISIONS_RESOLVED_20261029.md D8): CF's own requirement record
# cf_events_sem_eid (cf_events.h L148-L158, contract-backed, side caller) is the appreq, and P3 keeps the exit
# out of the allowed handling, so allowed is none: a not-ready lookup is VIOLATING (SPEC 1.6 step (1)).  The text
# above describes the earlier reading (appreq and allowed unspecified_by_reference).
phi 1;

rspec K-REG.osal-countsem-lookup {
  use op OS_CountSemGetIdByName;
  key osal.countsem(arg.sem_name);
  requires state(osal.countsem(arg.sem_name)) = LIVE;
  oracle fns "OS_ObjectIdFindByName", "OS_ObjectNameMatch";
  appreq cf_events_sem_eid;
  allowed none;
  harm app_error_exit;
  authored "2026-10-24, C1 profile, from SPEC_FINAL rev 1.3 1.6, 2.3 and App. A.4 steps 3 and 6, plan/C1_basis_plan.md 9.3, 9.7, 9.8; cases inspected: C1";
  prov cf_dox_flow_control, issue_184_body, cf_events_sem_eid, osal_countsem_h_getidbyname, cf_cfdp_lookup, cf_app_init_status, cf_app_exit;
}
